    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d701">

                <pb facs="0697" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">600.0031 World Program/157½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The King of the Belgians</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leopold III</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="23" xml:id="d701-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-25">25 July 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear President and Friend</hi>: My Prime Minister,
                    on his return from the United States, conveyed to me your kind message which
                    greatly touched me and for which I thank you most sincerely.</p>
                <p>He gave me an account of the conversation that you had with him: I was impressed
                    by what you said about the necessity to draw the world’s attention to something
                    quite new.</p>
                <p>I am taking this opportunity to send you the copy of a letter that I have just
                    addressed to Monsieur van Zeeland and I hope that you will consider with
                    interest the ideas that I have exposed in it.</p>
                <p>Believe me, dear President,</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Léopold</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d701-a1.xml" xpointer="d701-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
